        "id": 1380943
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-14T22:58:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Alternatively, i tried enabling CONFIG_CHIPSET_ICELAKE from zephyr nissa but did not help.\n\nCONFIG_CHIPSET_METEORLAKE is enabled for zephyr mtlrvp but when i compile the code for mtlrvp, i see the part of code under CONFIG_POWER_COMMON file usb_tc_drp_acc_trysrc_sm.c was not compiled.",
      "parentUuid": "67afd741_f07f932b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6505,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 6505,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "1566c01dab9d014ec133eda4a40f6de7de6665b1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ddaeb543_682180c1",
        "filename": "include/config.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 6505,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-14T23:16:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note that the options `CONFIG_CHIPSET_ICELAKE` and `CONFIG_CHIPSET_METEORLAKE` are not compatible with `CONFIG_AP_PWRSEQ`, which is used by the mtlrvpp_npcx and nissa boards.\n\n`CONFIG_AP_PWRSEQ` enables the new Zephyr based AP power sequence code https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/HEAD:src/platform/ec/zephyr/test/ap_power/src/ap_pwrseq.c;l\u003d1.\n\nNon-intel platforms use `CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_POWERSEQ` to use the legacy power sequence code: https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/HEAD:src/platform/ec/power/common.c;l\u003d1\n\nYou shouldn\u0027t need any changes to this file, as your change to Kconfig should force `CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_POWER_COMMON\u003dy`.  This code in the Zephyr shim should then automatically enable `CONFIG_POWER_COMMON`.\nhttps://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/HEAD:src/platform/ec/zephyr/shim/include/config_chip.h;l\u003d2724",
      "parentUuid": "33ccad0d_09505df0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6505,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 6505,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "1566c01dab9d014ec133eda4a40f6de7de6665b1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d53b7d35_904138c2",
        "filename": "include/config.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 6505,
      "author": {
        "id": 1281040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-15T00:33:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ICELAKE is not nissa. Nissa is ADL-N, selected in zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/Kconfig as CONFIG_X86_NON_DSX_PWRSEQ_ADL\n\nNote that CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_POWER_COMMON is only set for legacy power sequence code.\nThe new (ADL-N) power sequence code does not define that.\n\nIt may be that code or functionality from the legacy power code has not been ported to the new power sequence code - exactly what code from power/common.c is being referenced that is needed?",
      "parentUuid": "ddaeb543_682180c1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6505,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 6505,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "1566c01dab9d014ec133eda4a40f6de7de6665b1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e1aaf41c_4e83570f",
        "filename": "include/config.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 6505,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380943
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-15T00:54:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Below is the problem seen while enabling CONFIG_POWER_COMMON using CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_POWER_COMMON\u003dy in zephyr.\n\nin \"include/config.h\" file\nLine 5763 #include \"config_chip.h\"   \u003e\u003e zephyr configs are enabled here\nLine 6307 #undef CONFIG_POWER_COMMON \u003e\u003e this will override the zephyr configs enabled at line 5763 !!\n\nHence zephyr config CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_POWER_COMMON\u003dy is overwritten by config.h file.",
      "parentUuid": "d53b7d35_904138c2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6505,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 6505,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "1566c01dab9d014ec133eda4a40f6de7de6665b1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fc6aee5d_10aab6f8",
        "filename": "include/config.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 6505,
      "author": {
        "id": 1281040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-15T01:05:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_POWER_COMMON (and by derivation CONFIG_POWER_COMMON)\nshould only be set with the legacy power handling. It should not\nbe set when using the new power sequence code.\n\nThe code as it is works as intended, so CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_POWER_COMMON is only\nenabled when CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_POWERSEQ is enabled (this is the legacy power sequence).\n\nThe comment about enabling this for all Zephyr boards is wrong - this should only\nbe enabled for zephyr boards that use the legacy power sequence code. Zephyr boards using the new power sequence (Nissa etc.) should not define this.\n\nThe real question here is: what feature or functionality is required from power/common.c that is missing with the new power sequence code?",
      "parentUuid": "e1aaf41c_4e83570f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6505,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 6505,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "1566c01dab9d014ec133eda4a40f6de7de6665b1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
